WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:07.940
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:07.940
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.240
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.240
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.620
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.620
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.920
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.920
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.260
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.260
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.510
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.510
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.910
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.910
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:45.980
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:45.980
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:51.530
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:51.530
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.620
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.620
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.910
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.910
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:07.170
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:07.170
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:12.840
namida kareru made

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:12.840
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.890
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.890
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:23.230
namida hareru made

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:23.230
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:28.230
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:28.230
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.070
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.070
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.570
kizamu

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:39.330
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.860
akashi

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.330
kono te de

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:51.360
Here at the Indianapolis Braves Stadium, the game between the Wings and Hornets is drawing to a close.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.530
The Hornets entered the bottom of the ninth trailing by one.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:58.120
Keene made a single with no outs,

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.490
and the fourth batter, Parker, sent a fly ball to left field for the first out.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:07.750
Now Greene comes up to bat, having already made two hits.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.460
Play!

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.760
It's hit through to right field!

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:23.030
Keene advances to third base, and the Hornets are looking for a comeback with runners on first and third.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:27.950
Good, good.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.060
Now we can tie this up with a sacrifice fly.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.600
Don't mess this up.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.840
Boss,

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.840
shouldn't we call for a pinch hitter?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.920
Dunstan hasn't had any hits in the past few games.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.950
No, he's reliable.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.320
I'm sure he can hit a sacrifice fly.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.410
He's gone through tough times in the past, and he fixed his problems on his own.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.770
We should be patient with him.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.630
Let's see it, Dunstan!

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.730
Play!

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:03.450
Out!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.120
Out!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.290
A double play, and that ends the game!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.960
Dunstan has been struggling lately.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.980
We saw no hits from him today in his four at-bats.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.880
That puts an end to the Hornets' four-game win streak.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.680
What's your problem?!

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.020
Hey, Dunstan!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:30.100
The Entrusted Dream

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:30.100
The Entrusted Dream

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.770
Man, there goes our winning streak.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.210
Don't worry about it.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:40.160
We'll just start a new one.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.310
Don't be so greedy.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.650
Yeah, since this amazing rookie is making winning a piece of cake this year.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.290
Right, right.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.540
Keep dreaming.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.600
Oh, have you heard?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.630
The owner's thinking about reinforcing the team.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:55.820
Reinforcing the team?

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.420
This late in the season?

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:02.470
He's putting a lot of pressure on the boss, saying we need to win no matter what this year.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.640
I can't say I don't agree.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.590
We usually don't even come close to winning in our league,

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:13.030
but we're ranked pretty high since we started winning in the second half of the season.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.820
What I'm concerned about is the reinforcement.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.640
The owner could be looking to make a trade.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.550
If that happens, someone's leaving.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:26.010
The benchwarmers are still practicing after hearing the rumor.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.860
They're not the only possibility.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.150
I'm sure they wouldn't trade someone who's doing well,

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.620
so we really have to bring up our game.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.770
Man...

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:41.690
It's way too early to be talking about taking the title when we just started to win.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.180
It's never too early to be talking about taking the title.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.340
I'm always aiming to take it all.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.510
Nice one, future ace!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.770
Dinner's on you tonight.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.680
What?

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.430
You should treat your seniors from time to time.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.250
What?!

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.670
Thanks for the meal.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.480
Thanks, future ace.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.380
Hey, who said I'm paying?!

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.440
Let me go, damn it!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.850
If we start playing badly from hunger, we could get kicked off the team.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.240
If that were to happen, we'd blame you.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.200
That has nothing to do with me!

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.370
Don't let it get to you, Dunstan.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.770
It's just a rumor.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.580
I know.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.920
I'm not worried.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.820
Though I'll admit I'm not doing very well.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.720
See you tomorrow.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.470
What were you doing today?!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.020
We had momentum from four straight wins, so how did we lose?!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.020
I'm sorry.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.170
Especially the last batter!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.690
It was the perfect chance to tie or even make a comeback!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.880
Why didn't you call for a pinch hitter when you knew Dunstan was struggling?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.400
We have tons of players in the dugout!

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.380
We pay them for a reason!

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.110
But... Dunstan's...

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.280
Shut up!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.460
We're drawing a bigger crowd now that the Hornets are doing well.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:58.450
If the Hornets were to take the title for the first time in twenty-five years,

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:02.710
then we'd get even more media attention and even bigger crowds!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.010
Listen, Stacy, you're dead if you can't keep up our momentum.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.390
Yes, sir.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.810
Strike out!

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:20.550
Out!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.160
Don't throw so hard!

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.000
You're starting tomorrow.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.790
Don't worry about it.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.400
Yo, Greene.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.510
It's tough to do running drills at my age.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:00.240
You're our cleanup. You still have years ahead of you.

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:04.980
Nah, I can let our young and talented players do the work.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.130
That's true.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.910
I'll throw flaming balls and let you bathe in glory after winning every upcoming game.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.240
That's a big mouth you've got there.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.940
I have high hopes for you.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.080
Hopes, huh?

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.420
A friend of mine wanted to be a professional football player,

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:28.940
but he injured his knee and had to give up on that dream.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:34.680
I went back to Japan before this season, and you know what he told me?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.850
"Though you're not playing football, you're living my dream of being a professional athlete."

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:47.110
"So live that dream for both of us and become an even greater baseball player."

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.410
Your words kind of reminded me of that.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.580
So you have his dream on your shoulders too.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.290
I wouldn't exactly say that.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.120
It's just...

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.920
It makes me think his spirit is in every ball I pitch.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.840
I guess I'm saying I can't be sloppy.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.500
I see.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:14.610
I say that, but I was doing pretty badly in the first half of the season.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.010
Hey, Dunstan.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.810
The boss wants to see you.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.520
The Hornets are batting in the bottom of the first.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.260
Roy got on base with a walk, and now he's at third base.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:30.230
With two outs and a runner in scoring position, the fourth batter, Parker, is at bat.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.370
All right! First run!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.450
Good.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.830
We're doing well today.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.170
What's wrong, Dunstan?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.520
You haven't been batting very well lately.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.590
You're a consistent guy, so it's rare to see you in a rut for this long.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.010
The team's riding some momentum right now.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.710
I don't want to stop it.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:06.190
I'm going to switch you out for Klose starting tonight since he's shown good results as a pinch hitter.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.920
I'm sorry, but you'll have to sit out until you get your game back.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.230
I understand.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.200
What the hell am I doing,

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:21.620
when I've finally got a firm spot on a major league roster?

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.910
The second half of the game's become a complete hitting game.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:51.810
Yeah.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.770
Get on base, Robinson!

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.070
All right, it's through!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.110
A runner on and no outs!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.500
I'd like to have Carpenter pinch hit for Nelson.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.120
B-Boss?

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.820
We're going to be short on outfielders if you do that.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:08.850
I know that!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:09.760
It's the last inning.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:10.670
Let's hit it strong.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:13.800
Out!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:16.340
Damn!

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:18.180
Pinch hitter, Danforth.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.840
Another pinch hitter?

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.970
Hey...

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.100
What are we gonna do about the outfield if we don't score?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:26.850
Ball!

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:34.570
Listen, Stacy, you're dead if you can't keep up our momentum.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.160
Please, Danforth,

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.700
get on base.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.740
Strike!

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:48.750
This is a rare chance for us benchwarmers to show off our skills.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:52.480
I need to at least get a hit so I won't be traded.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.710
All right, it's thr—

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:57.890
Out!

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:58.790
Crap!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.100
Out!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.890
And the game continues.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.180
Just our luck.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.980
Boss, what should we do about defense?

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:12.310
Dunstan!

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:13.610
Yes?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.220
You used to play center field, right?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.280
Can you go out?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.800
Yes, sir.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.370
Greene, you take left field.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:21.740
S-Sure...

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.410
I can't feel comfortable in a position I don't usually play.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.750
Leave the left-center gap to me.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.660
Sure, it's all yours.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:39.590
I'll make up for my bad batting with defense.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.550
Strike two!

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.110
I've got it!

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:12.920
Greene!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.710
Is Greene all right?

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.000
Greene!

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:18.710
Get a stretcher!

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.520
G-Greene...

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:38.730
Greene's torn a ligament in his right knee.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:42.650
I don't think he'll be able to play for the rest of the season.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.030
It's unfortunate, but that's reality.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.950
We have to pull through the rest of the season without him.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.230
Don't let me down.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:53.810
Unbelievable...

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.910
That's unfortunate for Greene.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:13:01.340
He's not exactly young, so he may have to quit with an injury like that.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.170
Hey, that's going a bit too far.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.950
No, you never know.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.910
It's my fault.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.270
If I had just played normally...

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:15.190
It was my fault.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.670
Dunstan, that was an accident.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:20.100
It wasn't your fault at all.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.610
Watts is right.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.840
It's nothing for you to worry about.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.190
Come in.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.000
Dunstan.

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:45.710
Hey.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:01.160
The doctors don't want me to do this.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:05.440
I thought I'd train as much as I can so I'll be ready when my leg heals.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.880
I see.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.010
I know myself best.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:17.790
I may not be able to continue baseball this season, or even next season.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.300
Greene, what are you saying?

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.750
But...

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.050
I'm a professional.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:29.410
I can't just give up before the end.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:35.530
Greene.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:38.600
I'm sorry.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:42.040
If only... I had made a calm decision,

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.770
you wouldn't have been injured like this.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.820
Don't say that, Dunstan.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.900
We weren't in our normal positions.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.360
It's my fault too.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:55.060
How are you going to play baseball if you take things like this to heart?

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.710
Hey, don't make a face like that!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.170
Man, you're way too serious.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.460
I don't know about next season,

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:12.300
but it's a shame that I can't be in the dugout when we're so close to the championships.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:17.600
It took a while for me to get out of the minors.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:22.620
So, considering my age, I'm sure the Hornets will be my first and last major league team.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.060
So...

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:28.400
When the Hornets take the title, it'll be like a dream come true.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:30.450
Greene.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:34.080
What did I say about making that face, Dunstan?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.120
Play for me too, and show me the winning trophy with the Hornets.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:52.780
Strike out!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.340
Damn it!

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.520
Out!

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.220
Strike out!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.520
No runners again, huh...

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.000
It looks like this'll be a pitching game.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.240
You gonna be okay?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.030
Yeah.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.370
We can't lose anymore, so let's take it up a notch.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.240
Strike out!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:01.660
Safe!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.690
He's been pushing his limits, and his pitches are slowing down.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.600
Yeah.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.080
All right, let's switch pitchers.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:12.320
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 63:

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.760
Hagan!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.560
Damn it.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.480
I'm not meant to watch the game from the sidelines!

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:28.650
There must be something I can do.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.990
Safe! Safe!

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:42.120
What are you doing?

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.040
This is bad.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.710
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 21:

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.900
McDowell!

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.250
We can't lose anymore.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:03.130
Get on base, Roy.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.350
Play!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.500
Strike!

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.640
Why is Roy so tense?

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.310
That was a ball.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:16.520
Hey, Shigeno.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:23.450
The other day, you were telling Greene about your friend in Japan, right?

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.250
Yeah.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:29.930
What does it feel like to have someone's dream entrusted to you?

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:31.020
Huh?

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.610
What do you mean?

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:35.550
I went to visit Greene in the hospital yesterday.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:39.090
There, Greene entrusted his dream to me.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:42.220
His dream for the Hornets to take the title.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.580
Strike two!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.690
I don't even worry about how it feels.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:57.610
I think it's about doing your very best even if you're in a slump, so you don't destroy his dream.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.910
Believing in your own strength.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.830
Yeah, that's it.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:08.290
Ball!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.910
Roy, you need to relax!

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.150
Watch the ball!

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.650
The pitcher's throwing them a little high!

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.030
You're our leadoff batter!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:18.320
Your job is to get on base no matter what!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.920
What's going on?

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.930
Dunstan never gets this excited.

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:28.930
Ball.

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:30.560
Ball.

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:32.270
Ball.

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.240
Ball! Ball four!

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.150
Damn it.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.690
Good job, Roy!

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:39.690
I've got you to thank.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.910
Looks like I forgot my job.

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.120
Out!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.960
Nice bunt, Nelson!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:49.040
All right, a base hit could tie the game!

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:51.990
Ball! Ball four!

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.490
Good job, Keene!

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:55.340
Good judgement!

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:01.680
Even if I'm not playing in the game, there's still something I can do.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:04.600
I need to do all I can in every moment of the game.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:09.140
That's the only way I'll have a chance to get back in, let alone win the championships.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.480
Dead ball!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.110
The bases are loaded with one out.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.360
We should call in a pinch hitter.

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:24.270
Dunstan.

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:24.950
Yes?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.660
Even a fly to the outfield will score us a run.

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:29.160
Can you do it?

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.680
Go hit it big.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.630
Don't make me a losing pitcher.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.130
Sure, leave it to me.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:43.200
Attention, please. Batter, number 28:

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.720
Dunstan!

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:45.970
Play!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:53.550
Until today, I thought being a professional was about doing your job consistently.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.190
Strike!

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.150
Ball!

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.580
But...

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:03.570
I guess I was wrong.

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:15.120
Play for me too, and show me the winning trophy with the Hornets.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.550
Dunstan, let's go!

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:30.310
Shouldering another's dream is also part of being a pro!

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.480
Safe!

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:45.780
All right!

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.070
Follow his lead, guys!

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.220
Strike out!

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:56.660
Game over!

00:21:56.660 --> 00:22:00.130
The Hornets' batters made an explosive comeback in the top of the ninth!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:05.630
Then Watts closed it to end the game with a 5-1 comeback.

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.550
You did it, Dunstan.

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.170
Sheesh, that was a close call.

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:14.890
Come in.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:20.810
It's about the trade you asked me to make.

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:22.860
Oh, what's the news?

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:25.410
We simply need to formalize the contract.

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:27.350
He should be able to play in a few days.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:28.470
Really?

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:30.150
Good job.

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:35.150
This'll get us even bigger crowds.

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:59.290
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:59.290
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:04.610
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:04.610
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.990 --> 00:23:10.870
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.990 --> 00:23:10.870
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:15.660
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:15.660
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:22.290
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:22.290
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:28.130
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:28.130
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.970
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.970
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:39.390
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:39.390
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:45.860
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:45.860
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:51.110
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:54.580
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:54.580
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.040
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.580 --> 00:24:03.420
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:03.420
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.260
sotto

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.260
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.450
Preview

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.450
Preview

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:11.830
Say what?

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:15.520
I hear the new player's a pretty big troublemaker.

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:19.060
Well, if he'll contribute to the team with his skills,

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:21.390
then welcome, Mr. Troublemaker.

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:25.100
Next time, on Major: The Unspoken Rule

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.280
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.410
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.410
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.410
The Unspoken Rule

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:30.410
The Unspoken Rule
